  "final_text": "**Proposed disposition:** ESCALATE, with confidence 0.72.\n\n**The three facts that drove it:**\n1. The trader placed one BUY limit of 27,326 (11.15\u00d7 average depth) 2 ticks from the touch. It had no fills before the trader's SELL market order of 640. Only 4,707 filled afterwards, and the remaining 22,619 was cancelled 704 ms after the sale.\n2. The activity was one-sided (cancel symmetry 0.0). The trader is a prop trader with no market-making registration. There was no market event, no risk event, no parent order and no market-wide cancels, so none of the accepted explanations holds.\n3. The price moved 1 tick in the trader's favour and then reverted 1.5 ticks after the cancel.\n\n**Why not DRAFT_STOR:** This was a single cycle in the session (repetitions = 1) and the order-to-trade ratio was 1.0. That leaves it to Level 2 to assess.\n\n**What would change my mind:** Evidence that the BUY was a genuine working order, such as a client parent order, or that the SELL was an unrelated hedge.",
